Guard the <execinfo.h> stack-trace code so librm_lines builds on musl.

getStackTrace() uses backtrace()/backtrace_symbols() from <execinfo.h> on
every non-Windows platform. musl libc (Alpine) has no <execinfo.h>, so the
build fails there. Use the execinfo implementation only on glibc and Apple
platforms and return a placeholder string elsewhere. The stack trace is
only used for diagnostics, so nothing else changes.

Local patch against librm_lines 1.4.7, to be proposed upstream.
Tracking issue: https://github.com/jswent/rmfakecloud/issues/1

diff --git a/rm_lines/src/library.cpp b/rm_lines/src/library.cpp
index 44db74b..676e008 100644
--- a/rm_lines/src/library.cpp
+++ b/rm_lines/src/library.cpp
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@ std::string getStackTrace() {
 
     return std::string(buffer);
 }
-#else
+#elif defined(__GLIBC__) || defined(__APPLE__)
 #include <execinfo.h>
 
 std::string getStackTrace() {
@@ -126,4 +126,7 @@ std::string getStackTrace() {
     free(strings);
     return stackTrace.str();
 }
+#else
+// musl: no <execinfo.h>
+std::string getStackTrace() { return "<stack trace unavailable>"; }
 #endif
